-- A re-exported function carried after an interface method of the same name.
--
-- `facade` carries a's interface `Rend` (method `rendr`) ahead of b's function
-- `rendr`.  The front end binds the importer's `rendr` to b's function and warns
-- that the method shadows it inside `facade` (`W-IMPORT-METHOD-SHADOW`).  The fn
-- export map lets an interface-method origin yield to the later function origin,
-- so the reference names b's function symbol rather than none.
--
-- Expected output, derived by hand from the semantics: `rendr 1` is b's
-- `n + 1`, `2`.
import facade.{rendr}

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (intToString (rendr 1))
